    "description": "The Measure of Anxiety in Selection Interviews (MASI) is a 30-item self-report scale assessing the anxiety experienced by candidates during employment selection interviews. It is used in occupational and organizational research to study how interview-specific anxiety relates to performance and candidate outcomes.",
